      "content": "While naproxen may be helpful alongside sumatriptan, it's still important to speak with your healthcare provider before taking both medications together, particularly if your migraine is more severe than usual. A severe headache behaving like a thunderclap and intensified nausea are warning signs that could indicate something more serious than a typical migraine, such as a more dangerous condition like a subarachnoid hemorrhage. The ER checks are to ensure you receive the right care in time—for your peace of mind and health. If you really can't reach a professional, but your symptoms are escalating, it could be safer to go to the ER.",
      "source": "target",
